<title>GERMANY: Telefonica can't rule out intl tranche cut.</title>
<headline>Telefonica can't rule out intl tranche cut.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish telecommunications group Telefonica said on Friday it could not rule out a reduction in the international tranche of its forthcoming share sale.</p>
<p>&quot;We cannot rule that out. It can go further (below the 32 percent floor currently envisaged),&quot; said Telefonica chairman Juan Villalonga.</p>
<p>Villalonga, speaking at the first stage of an international road show, said the domestic retail tranche of the issue was currently some seven times oversubscribed.</p>
<p>The Spanish state is due to sell its remaining 20.9 percent stake in the firm, with final pricing of the issue scheduled for February 17.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
